>>> j = dumps(data, cls=PythonObjectEncoder)

>>> loads(j, object_hook=as_python_object)
[1, 2, 3, set(['knights', 'say', 'who', 'ni']), {'key': 'value'}, Decimal('3.14')]
```

Alternatively, it may be useful to use a more general purpose serialization technique such as [YAML](http://yaml.org/), [Twisted Jelly](http://twistedmatrix.com/documents/8.1.0/api/twisted.spread.jelly.html), or Python's [pickle module](http://docs.python.org/library/pickle.html#module-pickle).  These each support a much greater range of datatypes.

